decisions:
  - closed mutation operator enum values are `targeted-behavior-change`, `repair`, `simplify`, `performance-tune`, `guardrail-change`, `tool-strategy-change`, `model-routing-change`, `prompt-policy-change`, `hill-climb` and `exploratory-leap`
  - TOON remains the reviewable contract envelope; canonical S-expression is the internal mutation/operator IR
  - Git diff is candidate realization evidence, not the mutation itself
  - conceptual crossover recombines evidence-backed parent traits into a new bounded child mutation contract using the closed enum
  - hill-climb and exploratory-leap require search posture: parent candidate, objective focus, expected delta and risk budget
  - fitness scoring is deterministic, evidence-only, hard-gated, then weighted; promotion threshold is `0.80`

files:
  - path: application/src/test/java/com/dreamthought/saaa/application/MutationOperatorTypeTest.java
    reason: asserts closed enum parsing and deterministic defaults
  - path: application/src/test/java/com/dreamthought/saaa/application/MutationContractCanonicalizerTest.java
    reason: asserts canonical S-expression shape and jqwik atom normalization
  - path: application/src/test/java/com/dreamthought/saaa/application/MutationContractValidatorTest.java
    reason: asserts bounded targeted contract validation and rejection messages
  - path: application/src/test/java/com/dreamthought/saaa/application/SearchPosturePolicyTest.java
    reason: asserts hill-climb and exploratory-leap posture controls
  - path: application/src/test/java/com/dreamthought/saaa/application/ConceptualCrossoverPolicyTest.java
    reason: asserts conceptual crossover creates a bounded child contract, not an enum operator or diff merge
  - path: application/src/test/java/com/dreamthought/saaa/application/PhenotypeFitnessScorerTest.java
    reason: asserts hard-gated phenotype scoring and threshold promotion
  - path: core/src/main/java/com/dreamthought/saaa/core/
