  - path: application/src/main/java/com/dreamthought/saaa/application/
    reason: add deterministic policies here
  - path: specs/changes/CHG-002-live-loop-policy/change.toon
    reason: update T3, T3b, T3c and T4 status when tests pass; leave T2/T5/T6 pending and T7 deferred unless intentionally delivered

implementation_notes:
  - likely core types: `MutationOperatorType`, `FitnessObjective`, `MutationBounds`, `MutationTarget`, `SearchPosture`, `ParentTrait`, `MutationContract`
  - likely application types: `MutationOperatorPolicy`, `MutationOperatorDefaults`, `MutationContractCanonicalizer`, `MutationContractValidator`, `PhenotypeFitnessScorer`, `PhenotypeEvidence`, `BehaviorCaseEvidence`, `ConceptualCrossoverPolicy`, `ConceptualCrossoverRequest`
  - canonical atoms should be lower-case and hyphenated; underscores become hyphens; quote file paths and parent trait prose
  - keep canonicalizer generation-only for now; a parser can be added later when needed
  - validator can reuse the authority-boundary idea from `BoundedMutationValidator` but should not depend on LangChain4j or infrastructure
  - targeted behavior default bounds expected by tests are `max_files_changed=2`, `max_lines_changed=80`, and no public API, persistence or production config changes
  - fitness objectives expected by tests are `task_success=0.40`, `reliability=0.20`, `cost_latency_budget=0.20`, `behavioral_safety=0.10`, `parsimony=0.10`
  - if hard gates fail, `PhenotypeFitnessScorer` should discard and report aggregate score `0.0`

risks:
  - because tests are unrun, there may be small compile/import expectation mismatches to correct
  - implementing every possible validation rule from `CHG-002` would overbuild; satisfy the named tests and keep policy extensible
  - conceptual crossover test touches a deferred capability; keep it as deterministic child-contract generation only, not loop integration or diff crossover
  - direct main shipping still requires branch isolation, deterministic checks, actor review or recorded fallback, lead self-review and explicit user authorization under `AGENTS.md`

ask_before:
  - destructive cleanup or deleting dirty work
  - force push
  - broad implementation beyond the new tests
  - direct merge to `main` if local validation or actor review is unavailable
